WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.402 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is
a zombie-apocalypse movie

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:04.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
with a fantastic cast.
-Yeah.

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:06.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Adam Driver, Bill Murray,
Tilda Swinton,

00:00:06.106 --> 00:00:07.707 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Chloe Sevigny, yourself.

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:08.675 line:92%
Jim Jarmusch directed it.

00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:12.278 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is not a man who is known
for his zombie films.

00:00:12.278 --> 00:00:15.081 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, he's not.
-Yeah.

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:16.282 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-By the way, that clip

00:00:16.282 --> 00:00:18.752 size:78% position:39%
was just from footage
of my house upstate.

00:00:18.752 --> 00:00:20.820 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-I don't know how you got that

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's me every morning.
-I'm so sorry.

00:00:22.389 --> 00:00:24.524
They told us that was from
the movie, but that's just -

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:27.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's actual documentary-film
footage of you...

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:28.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-...and your farm.

00:00:28.228 --> 00:00:31.598 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, I feel terrible.
We have violated your privacy,

00:00:31.598 --> 00:00:32.632 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I apologize.
-That's okay.

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:34.200
But you -- you do play a farmer.
-Yes.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:37.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you sort of --
I guess, as that clip tells us

00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:38.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
you might realize
something's wrong

00:00:38.338 --> 00:00:39.572 line:92%
'cause your animals go missing

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:41.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Something's going on
in the town.

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:43.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-It's very troubling, yes.

00:00:43.243 --> 00:00:44.444 line:92%
-There's a lot of prosthetic

00:00:44.444 --> 00:00:47.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
as you would expect
from a zombie film.

00:00:47.247 --> 00:00:50.383 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you enjoy
that part of the job?

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:51.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
-Yeah.

00:00:51.384 --> 00:00:52.619 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:52.619 --> 00:00:55.155 line:92%
-Yeah, I mean, everybody's nice,

00:00:55.155 --> 00:00:56.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
but it takes a long time..

00:00:56.189 --> 00:00:58.158 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-...to put the makeup on.

00:00:58.158 --> 00:01:00.093 line:92%
And then you look like a zombie,

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:01.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
and nobody wants
to talk to you, really.

00:01:01.928 --> 00:01:03.963 size:84% position:42%
-Did you feel same way
about your cast members

00:01:03.963 --> 00:01:05.398 align:start size:94% position:6%
who were the zombies?
-Yeah.

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:09.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, Chloe Sevigny
is in the film,

00:01:09.069 --> 00:01:10.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I hadn't seen her
in a long time,

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:13.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we were catching up.
But -- And I --

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:14.908 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
having a serious conversation,

00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:16.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I couldn't
look her in the eye

00:01:16.309 --> 00:01:19.546
'cause, literally, her eye was
like, falling out of her head.

00:01:19.546 --> 00:01:20.213 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.213 --> 00:01:21.714 align:start size:94% position:6%
Had to stop talking.
-Yeah, it's very hard to -

00:01:21.714 --> 00:01:23.550
Somebody you haven't seen
in 10 years and you have to say,

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:24.851 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You look great..."
-Yeah, right.

00:01:24.851 --> 00:01:29.155
-"...you haven't aged a day,
with like a dead, lolling eye.

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:30.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
Bill Murray's
one of your co-stars.

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:32.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
Have you work together before?
-Never.

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:34.527 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But you did --
You auditioned for him.

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:37.964
-I did.
You know, he co-directed a film,

00:01:37.964 --> 00:01:39.899 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Quick Change."
-Yeah, fantastic film.

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:44.137
-And I auditioned for it.
I didn't get the part.

00:01:44.137 --> 00:01:50.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
But he told me
when I came in that --

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:52.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
He said,
"We looked at your picture

00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:55.782 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you sort of
look like a psycho."

00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:57.150 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.150 --> 00:02:00.920
"And you come in here, and you
really do look like a psycho."

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:01.488 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.488 --> 00:02:04.457
"It's just most people
don't look like their pictures."

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:06.159 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's so nice.
-I said, "Thank you."

00:02:06.159 --> 00:02:06.759 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-But this is true.

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:08.194 align:start size:94% position:6%
In your early days,
you had two head shots.

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:09.696 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I did, yeah.
-And so you would decide,

00:02:09.696 --> 00:02:12.999
based on the role, whether
to send out the psycho one

00:02:12.999 --> 00:02:15.168 size:84% position:42%
-Well, I didn't think
I looked like a psycho.

00:02:15.168 --> 00:02:19.205 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, I'm sorry.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:21.908 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, here --
This is obviously your --

00:02:21.908 --> 00:02:25.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. That's like, you know
like...the boy next door.

00:02:25.612 --> 00:02:27.213 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Boy next door.
-You know.

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:28.681 line:92%
-And this is the guy who maybe

00:02:28.681 --> 00:02:30.583 align:start size:94% position:6%
has some trouble
with the boy next door.

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:31.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-I mean, that's --

00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:34.354 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:34.354 --> 00:02:37.524
I mean, that's the same gu
but very different parts.

00:02:37.524 --> 00:02:38.491 line:92%
-But here's the weird thing.

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:40.693 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's how I really
preferred to look.

00:02:40.693 --> 00:02:42.428 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, I --
It was the '80s, you know,

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:44.664 align:start size:94% position:6%
so, like, a lot of hair gel.
-A lot of hair gel.

00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:46.533 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's how I walked around.
Yeah.

00:02:46.533 --> 00:02:50.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You found your first --
This is your first --

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:52.605 align:start size:94% position:6%
what would you say? --
your acting résumé?

00:02:52.605 --> 00:02:53.673 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that...?
-Yeah.

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:57.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And not a lot going on here
-No, it's very slight.

00:02:57.443 --> 00:02:58.778 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:58.778 --> 00:02:59.946 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-Is it true that you --

00:02:59.946 --> 00:03:01.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause you did
some stand-up comedy.

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:02.815 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I did.
-But in your early days,

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:04.817 size:78% position:39%
you actually thought
there was a chance --

00:03:04.817 --> 00:03:07.820 align:start size:94% position:6%
Ventriloquism
was a thing you took.

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:08.855 line:92%
-You know, when I was a kid,

00:03:08.855 --> 00:03:11.324
you know,
I wanted to be in show business.

00:03:11.324 --> 00:03:12.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-You know, I didn't necessaril

00:03:12.859 --> 00:03:15.962 align:start size:94% position:6%
know, like, how to be an actor
but I figured,

00:03:15.962 --> 00:03:17.330 line:92%
you gotta know a lot of stuff.

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:19.499 line:92%
So I learned how to juggle

00:03:19.499 --> 00:03:21.334 align:start size:94% position:6%
I learned
how to ride a unicycle.

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:22.135 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:22.135 --> 00:03:23.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, I --
for a little while,

00:03:23.636 --> 00:03:26.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
I thought, "Ventriloquism --
that's my ticket."

00:03:26.639 --> 00:03:28.942 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then, did you realize
that it was the '80s

00:03:28.942 --> 00:03:31.511
and none of those skills
actually mattered anymore?

00:03:31.511 --> 00:03:32.879 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:34.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was so disappointed.
-Yeah.

00:03:34.614 --> 00:03:35.782 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Years of training.

00:03:35.782 --> 00:03:37.383 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But then, the good news was
you know, you thought,

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:39.252
oh, you wasted all that time
learning how to do that stuff,

00:03:39.252 --> 00:03:41.454
and in the end, they were like
"You know what's good, though?

00:03:41.454 --> 00:03:43.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
You look a little bit
like a psycho."

00:03:43.089 --> 00:03:44.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yes.

00:03:44.524 --> 00:03:45.792 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-"We can use that."

00:03:45.792 --> 00:03:49.128 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, you were doing stand-up,
and at the same

00:03:49.128 --> 00:03:50.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you were doing stand-up
and you were acting,

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:52.565 align:start size:94% position:6%
you were also a fireman.
-I was.

00:03:52.565 --> 00:03:54.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And not like
a volunteer fireman.

00:03:54.634 --> 00:03:55.435 line:92%
You were an actual fireman

00:03:55.435 --> 00:03:59.839 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, at Engine 55
in Manhattan, and I did that -

00:03:59.839 --> 00:04:05.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thank you.

00:04:05.345 --> 00:04:06.446 line:92%
I kind of kept it under wraps.

00:04:06.446 --> 00:04:08.081 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I had done
a little bit of stand-up,

00:04:08.081 --> 00:04:09.482 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then I got called
for the job,

00:04:09.482 --> 00:04:12.118 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I stopped doing stand-up,
and I just so --

00:04:12.118 --> 00:04:14.721 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was, like, the quietes
guy in the firehouse

00:04:14.721 --> 00:04:17.557 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause you didn't want
to give these guys

00:04:17.557 --> 00:04:20.126 align:start size:94% position:6%
any ammunition
to make fun of you.

00:04:20.126 --> 00:04:20.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure.
-Yeah.

00:04:20.793 --> 00:04:22.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, it was like --
So you would never say, like

00:04:22.695 --> 00:04:25.732
with everybody, "Did anybody
else here ride a unicycle?

00:04:25.732 --> 00:04:26.966 size:78% position:39% line:92%
You wouldn't -- yeah.

00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:28.868 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:32.905
-And there was only one other --
there was another firefighte

00:04:32.905 --> 00:04:34.507 align:start size:94% position:6%
that was an actor who worked
in another firehouse.

00:04:34.507 --> 00:04:38.478
His name was Dean Tulipane
and -- and they made fun of him.

00:04:38.478 --> 00:04:40.213 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like -- Like, night and day.
You know?

00:04:40.213 --> 00:04:42.749
And so I definitely wasn't
gonna tell anybody that I --

00:04:42.749 --> 00:04:44.917 size:75% position:38%
And then, I met him.
And because I lived

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:47.820 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the East Village,
he knew something was up.

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:49.956
He said, "What are you --
You must be something.

00:04:49.956 --> 00:04:51.557 align:start size:94% position:6%
A musician?
Are you an actor?"

00:04:51.557 --> 00:04:53.092 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I admitted
that I was an actor,

00:04:53.092 --> 00:04:54.694 line:92%
or that I wanted to be an actor.

00:04:54.694 --> 00:04:56.095 size:75% position:38%
And then, so the cat
was out of the bag.

00:04:56.095 --> 00:04:58.564
-And then they found out.
-And they tortured me.

00:04:58.564 --> 00:04:59.999 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And they tortured you.
[ Light laughter ]

00:04:59.999 --> 00:05:02.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you met -- Is it true
you met Jim Jarmusch,

00:05:02.468 --> 00:05:05.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
the director of this film,
as a stand-up?

00:05:05.238 --> 00:05:07.440 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, yes.
I was doing --

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:08.808 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Well, not stand-up.

00:05:08.808 --> 00:05:11.444
I had a partner, Mark Boone Jr.,
and we used to write --

00:05:11.444 --> 00:05:13.880 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Who's a great actor.
-He's a wonderful actor.

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:16.983
And we used to write and perform
our own material.

00:05:16.983 --> 00:05:20.019 line:92%
And we used to do this show.

00:05:20.019 --> 00:05:22.255 align:start size:94% position:6%
There was a comedian
called Rockets Redglare.

00:05:22.255 --> 00:05:23.323 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
-Did you ever know him?

00:05:23.323 --> 00:05:25.825 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No. Rockets -- His name
was Rockets Redglare?

00:05:25.825 --> 00:05:26.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Rockets Redglare.
-Okay.

00:05:26.893 --> 00:05:30.129 size:81% position:41%
-And he used to do --
-Got to go into comedy

00:05:30.129 --> 00:05:31.831 align:start size:94% position:6%
with a name like that.
I mean...

00:05:31.831 --> 00:05:33.466 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:33.466 --> 00:05:34.233 line:92%
-And he had a show called

00:05:34.233 --> 00:05:36.869 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Rockets Redglare's
Taxi's Cabaret."

00:05:36.869 --> 00:05:39.472 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Boone and I
would perform in that,

00:05:39.472 --> 00:05:41.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Jim used to see us in that
and that's how he cast me

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:46.713 align:start size:94% position:6%
in one of the early films,
"Mystery Train."

00:05:46.713 --> 00:05:48.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And -- And then,

00:05:48.114 --> 00:05:50.917 align:start size:94% position:6%
right after "Mystery Train,"
the day we wrapped --

00:05:50.917 --> 00:05:53.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
the next day,
we filmed a little short

00:05:53.119 --> 00:05:55.154 align:start size:94% position:6%
that he used for
"Coffee and Cigarettes"

00:05:55.154 --> 00:05:56.356 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
years later.

00:05:56.356 --> 00:05:58.458 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I hadn't worked with him
in 30 years.

00:05:58.458 --> 00:06:00.026 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's fantastic.
-Yeah.

00:06:00.026 --> 00:06:00.760 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-It's a great film.

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:02.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's great to see you guys
collaborate again.

00:06:02.161 --> 00:06:03.596
It's always such a pleasur
to have you here and see you

00:06:03.596 --> 00:06:06.265 size:75% position:38%
-Thank you, so much.
-Thank you, so much.

